</div>
<div align="left"> <br />
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font color="#ff0000"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4" style="font-size:
16pt;"><strong>August 29, 2007</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font color="#0000ff"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="4"><strong>HUMOR</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;"><br />
<br />
</font></font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><strong>RULES OF THE AIR FOR
PILOTS</strong></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif">1. 
E</font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2" style="font-size:
11pt;">very takeoff is optional. Every landing is
mandatory.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">2. Flying isn't dangerous. Crashing is
what's dangerous.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">3. It's always better to be down here
wishing you were up there than being up there wishing you were down
here.<br />
<br />
4. The ONLY time you have too much fuel is when you're on
fire.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">5.The propeller is just a big fan in
front of the plane used to keep the pilot cool. When it stops, you can
actually watch the pilot start sweating.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">6. A 'good' landing is one from which you
can walk away. A 'great' landing is one after which they can use the plane
again.<br />
<br />
7. Always try to keep the number of landings you make equal to the number
of take-offs you've made.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">8  You start with a bag full of luck and
an empty bag of experience.  The trick is to fill the bag of experience
before you empty the bag of luck.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">9.  In the ongoing battle between objects
made of aluminum going hundreds of miles per hour and the ground going zero
miles per hour, the ground has yet to lose.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">10.  Good judgment comes from experience.
Unfortunately, the experience usually comes from bad
judgment.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">.....</font></font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2">A
Joke A Day Ministries - </font></font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">Keith Todd</font></font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2"> (</font></font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">ktodd@vci.net) </font></font><font color="#000000"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2">by way of &quot;Christian
Voices&quot; (www.ChristianVoicesWorldwide.com)</font></font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font color="#ff0000"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4"><strong>&lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt;
  &lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt; 
 &lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt;  
&lt;&gt;&lt;</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font color="#0000ff"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4"><strong>THOUGHT PROVOKING &ndash;
INSPIRATIONAL</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><strong>Tug Of War</strong></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;">&ldquo;<font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>If any of you lacks wisdom, he should ask
God, who gives generously to all without finding
fault,</em></font></font></p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>and it will be given to him.&rdquo; -James
1:5</em></font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">When I was a small child I used to love
playing tug of war.  In case you are not familiar with this simple game,
one or more individuals pull on a long piece of rope which has a tie in the
middle of it, and each side&rsquo;s goal is to try to pull the other side
past a line that has been marked on the ground.  The side with the longer
end of rope wins.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Did you know that we all are involved in
a game of tug of war?  Not a fun game, mind you, but a spiritual war
between the forces of good and evil.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;">&ldquo;<font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>Put on the full armor of God so that you can
take your stand against the devil's schemes. For our</em></font></font></p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>struggle is not against flesh and blood, but
against the rulers, against the authorities, against the
powers</em></font></font></p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>of this dark world and against the spiritual
forces of evil in the heavenly realms.&rdquo;  -Ephesians
6:11-12</em></font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">As the above Bible verse suggests, we
need to be cautious and take heed so we do not unwittingly fall prey to
satan&rsquo;s wiles.  Part of the spiritual armor we must prepare ourselves
with is wisdom.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Why wisdom?</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Because we need to know who the players
are; who is the good guy, and who is the bad guy.  Since satan is a
deceiver, he will use tactics which may make us think his ways are the
right ways, but they are not, for as the Bible reveals, his purpose is to
steal away our salvation.  </font></font> </p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;">&ldquo;<font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>Be self-controlled and alert. Your enemy the
devil prowls around like a roaring lion</em></font></font></p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>looking for someone to devour.&rdquo;  -I
Peter 5:8</em></font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Wisdom is so important that the Bible
refers to it as better than precious rubies!</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;">&ldquo;<font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>For wisdom is more precious than rubies, and
nothing you desire can compare with her.&rdquo; -Proverbs
8:11</em></font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><a name="OLE_LINK2"></a><a
name="OLE_LINK1"></a> <font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">.....Melanie Schurr (editor@melanieschurr.com)
(www.MelanieSchurr.com) by way of </font></font><font color="#000000"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2">&quot;Christian Voices&quot;
(www.ChristianVoicesWorldwide.com)</font></font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font color="#ff0000"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4"><strong>&lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt;
  &lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt; 
 &lt;&gt;&lt;   &lt;&gt;&lt;  
&lt;&gt;&lt;</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;"><br />
</font></font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><strong>Shrimp
Boats</strong></font></p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>John 3:16 For God so loved the world that He
gave His only begotten Son, that whosoever believes in Him should not
perish, but have everlasting life.</em></font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Shrimp is one of my favorite shellfish.
After they are netted, brought in and prepared, they can be used in so many
ways.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">While in Savannah, I saw a lot of shrimp
boats, bobbing along in the Atlantic Ocean, busily doing their job. As I
looked out the window and watched several of these boats I was intrigued. 
They seemed to move at such a leisurely pace, going steadily on course,
with their nets sunk deep below the waters' surface. The booms extended
from each side of the boat, keeping the nets in the proper position to
catch those shrimp.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0.17in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">I thought, that is like God... moving
along in this world at His steady pace, with His arms extended wide, like
those shrimp booms. He is ready and willing to scoop us up into His arms of
love- to gather us unto Himself.  After we are gathered unto Him, we, like
the shrimp, can be used in so many ways to further His kingdom on earth.
No, we won't be peeled, breaded, boiled, or baked, but we will be used in a
special plan He has devised just for us. Isn't it a blessing that you have
been scooped up in God's net of unending and everlasting
love?</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">.....Marion Smith (noles65@aol.com)</font></font><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2"> </font></font><font
color="#000000"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2">by way of
&quot;Christian Voices&quot;
(www.ChristianVoicesWorldwide.com)</font></font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>                                    </div>
